---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import atifMeta from "../../public/data/evals/atif-smoke-0.40.0-next.0.meta.json";

const basePath = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
const harborCommit = "dc933be707feafbb9efcdf092cb8a0e391332617";
const ciWorkflow =
  "https://github.com/veasel-labs/veasel/blob/main/.github/workflows/ci.yml";
const harborDoc =
  "https://github.com/veasel-labs/veasel/blob/main/docs/compatibility/harbor.md";
const validateScript =
  "https://github.com/veasel-labs/veasel/blob/main/scripts/validate-harbor-atif.py";
const smokeReadme =
  "https://github.com/veasel-labs/veasel/blob/main/benchmarks/harbor/smoke-task/README.md";
const adapter =
  "https://github.com/veasel-labs/veasel/blob/main/benchmarks/harbor/veasel_agent.py";
const benchmarking =
  "https://github.com/veasel-labs/veasel/blob/main/docs/benchmarking.md";
const atifSampleHref = `${basePath}/data/evals/atif-smoke-0.40.0-next.0.json`;
const atifMetaHref = `${basePath}/data/evals/atif-smoke-0.40.0-next.0.meta.json`;
const mockProvider =
  "https://github.com/veasel-labs/veasel/blob/main/scripts/mock-provider.py";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Evaluations and ATIF traces"
  description="Honest status of Veasel ATIF trajectory validation, Harbor smoke coverage, and Harbor Index submission prep — no invented scores."
>
  <section class="doc-page evals-page">
    <p class="kicker">
      <span class="sparkle" aria-hidden="true">
        ✳
      </span>{" "}
      EVALS / HONEST STATUS
    </p>
    <h1>
      Traces when we can.
      <br />
      <em>Scores when we earn them.</em>
    </h1>
    <p class="lede">
      This page records what evaluation infrastructure exists today, what CI
      proves, and what is still unpublished. It does not invent leaderboard
      results or fabricate model runs.
    </p>

    <aside class="compatibility-banner" role="note">
      <span class="compatibility-mark" aria-hidden="true">
        ⌀
      </span>
      <div>
        <strong>Harbor Index: Not submitted</strong>
        <p>
          Veasel is <strong>not</strong> in Harbor’s built-in agent registry and
          has no Index trial set or leaderboard placement. A local{" "}
          <code>BaseInstalledAgent</code> adapter and CI ATIF validation exist;
          upstream Index work stays open — see the blockers and prep package
          below. This is not a claim of Index support.
        </p>
      </div>
    </aside>

    <aside class="compatibility-banner" role="note">
      <span class="compatibility-mark" aria-hidden="true">
        ✳
      </span>
      <div>
        <strong>Public ATIF smoke sample (sanitized)</strong>
        <p>
          A real four-step <code>ATIF-v1.8</code> trajectory from Veasel{" "}
          <code>{atifMeta.veasel_version}</code> + the deterministic{" "}
          <a href={mockProvider}>mock-provider</a> path (same contract Linux CI
          validates, then discards). Harbor <code>0.24.0</code> validator passed
          locally. This is <strong>plumbing only</strong> — not an Index trial
          and not a capability score.{" "}
          <a href={atifSampleHref}>Download sample JSON</a>
          {" · "}
          <a href={atifMetaHref}>Provenance</a>
          {" · "}
          SHA-256 <code>{atifMeta.sha256.slice(0, 16)}…</code>
        </p>
      </div>
    </aside>

    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>What CI proves today</h2>
      <ul class="guide-list">
        <li>
          Job <strong>Harbor installed-agent adapter</strong> unit-tests{" "}
          <a href={adapter}>
            <code>veasel_agent.py</code>
          </a>{" "}
          against the pinned Harbor agent API (<a href={ciWorkflow}>ci.yml</a>).
        </li>
        <li>
          Linux backend job: after <code>scripts/api-smoke.sh</code>, checkout
          Harbor at <code>{harborCommit.slice(0, 12)}</code> and run{" "}
          <a href={validateScript}>
            <code>scripts/validate-harbor-atif.py</code>
          </a>{" "}
          on the smoke trajectory.
        </li>
        <li>
          Uploaded CI artifacts include platform binaries,{" "}
          <code>benchmark-session-store</code>, and Trivy results —{" "}
          <strong>not</strong> ATIF JSON (CI still discards the raw smoke
          trace). The public sample above is a separately regenerated,
          path-scrubbed copy of that same deterministic path.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Methodology and redaction rules:{" "}
        <a href={benchmarking}>docs/benchmarking.md</a>. Adapter contract:{" "}
        <a href={harborDoc}>docs/compatibility/harbor.md</a>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>Recorded session path</h2>
      <p>What you can inspect today:</p>
      <ul class="guide-list">
        <li>
          Authentic{" "}
          <a href={`${basePath}/demo/`}>terminal asciinema on /demo/</a> from
          the <code>0.41.0-next.0</code> binary (CLI + scripted TUI keys; no
          live model).
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href={atifSampleHref}>Sanitized ATIF smoke JSON</a> (download) with{" "}
          <a href={atifMetaHref}>method + SHA-256</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          Interactive <a href={`${basePath}/demo/`}>product walkthrough</a>{" "}
          (labeled script of shipped commands — not a live model run).
        </li>
        <li>
          Full Harbor installed-agent smoke locally with{" "}
          <a href={smokeReadme}>
            <code>benchmarks/harbor/smoke-task</code>
          </a>{" "}
          and an exact published <code>VEASEL_VERSION</code>; inspect the job
          directory on your machine and do not publish unsanitized traces.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <pre class="evals-pre"><code># From a veasel checkout, after a verified release exists:
VEASEL_VERSION=0.40.0-next.0 benchmarks/harbor/smoke.sh
# Inspect the Harbor job directory locally — do not upload raw ATIF.</code></pre>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>Harbor Index — blockers (evidence)</h2>
      <p>
        Index submission was <strong>not</strong> performed from this
        workstation. Exact blockers checked 2026-10-15:
      </p>
      <ol class="guide-list evals-checklist">
        <li>
          <span class="evals-check open">Block</span>{" "}
          <code>harbor auth status</code> → <strong>Not authenticated</strong>.
          Hub upload / leaderboard flows need interactive{" "}
          <code>harbor auth login</code> (GitHub OAuth) or a stored{" "}
          <code>HARBOR_API_KEY</code> / <code>~/.harbor/credentials.json</code>.
          Neither is available in this agent environment.
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="evals-check open">Block</span> No authorized budget or
          org approval for an 80-task Harbor Index trial set (paid model calls +
          Hub job upload). Policy: no unpaid leaderboard claims.
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="evals-check open">Block</span> Harbor contribution policy
          requires a <strong>human-authored</strong> initial and final upstream
          PR draft for built-in agent registry changes. An automated agent must
          not open that PR.
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>Harbor Index — strongest prep package (not a submission)</h2>
      <p>
        Status remains <strong>Not submitted</strong>. Package contents for a
        future human maintainer — not Index placement:
      </p>
      <ul class="guide-list">
        <li>
          <strong>Adapter:</strong>{" "}
          <a href={adapter}>
            <code>benchmarks/harbor/veasel_agent.py</code>
          </a>{" "}
          (<code>BaseInstalledAgent</code>, Harbor <code>0.24.0</code> @{" "}
          <code>{harborCommit.slice(0, 12)}</code>).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Deterministic plumbing trial:</strong>{" "}
          <a href={smokeReadme}>
            <code>benchmarks/harbor/smoke-task</code>
          </a>{" "}
          via{" "}
          <code>VEASEL_VERSION=0.40.0-next.0 benchmarks/harbor/smoke.sh</code>{" "}
          (fixture model; reward plumbing only — not an Index score).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Public ATIF evidence:</strong>{" "}
          <a href={atifSampleHref}>atif-smoke-0.40.0-next.0.json</a> validated
          with Harbor’s trajectory models.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>
            Contribution PR draft (outline only — human must write):
          </strong>{" "}
          propose registering a custom installed agent that downloads the
          verified Linux release, maps Harbor providers honestly, writes ATIF to
          the agent log path, and documents autonomous opt-in + Bubblewrap
          requirements. Open a design discussion before interface changes per
          Harbor policy.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Index trial set (not started):</strong> pin Harbor Index
          dataset digest + agent image + model/provider + env revisions; run
          under authenticated Hub org with recorded uncertainty — only after
          budget + human PR path clear.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <ol class="guide-list evals-checklist">
        <li>
          <span class="evals-check done">Done</span> Local{" "}
          <code>BaseInstalledAgent</code> adapter + provider mapping honesty.
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="evals-check done">Done</span> Pin Harbor{" "}
          <code>0.24.0</code> / <code>{harborCommit.slice(0, 12)}</code>; CI
          ATIF validator gate.
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="evals-check done">Done</span> Deterministic smoke task
          (fixture model; not a coding benchmark).
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="evals-check done">Done</span> Sanitized public ATIF smoke
          sample linked above with provenance.
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="evals-check open">Open</span> Discuss interface/core
          changes with Harbor maintainers per their contribution policy.
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="evals-check open">Open</span> Human-authored initial and
          final upstream PR drafts (Harbor policy).
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="evals-check open">Open</span> Authorized Index trial set
          with recorded dataset/agent/model/env revisions — no unpaid
          leaderboard claims.
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <p class="doc-next">
      <a class="text-link" href={`${basePath}/benchmarks/`}>
        Startup measurements <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </a>
      <a class="text-link" href={`${basePath}/demo/`}>
        Product walkthrough <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </a>
      <a class="text-link" href={harborDoc}>
        Harbor compatibility note <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
      </a>
    </p>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>

<style>
  .evals-page {
    max-width: 820px;
  }
  .evals-page > h1 em {
    color: var(--green);
  }
  .evals-pre {
    margin: 16px 0 0;
    padding: 14px 16px;
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: #1c1f2e;
    color: #e8e6df;
    overflow-x: auto;
    font: 500 0.82rem/1.55 var(--mono);
  }
  .evals-checklist {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
  }
  .evals-checklist li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: auto 1fr;
    gap: 12px;
    align-items: start;
  }
  .evals-check {
    display: inline-block;
    min-width: 3.4rem;
    padding: 2px 8px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    font: 600 0.62rem var(--mono);
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .evals-check.done {
    background: var(--mint);
    color: var(--green-dark);
  }
  .evals-check.open {
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--line) 70%, var(--surface));
    color: var(--muted);
  }
</style>
